"THE AGREEMENT LAW. The kernel holds every row today`s lambda holds, and beyond them exactly the rows ka:allowed_extra names, each population with its count: ka:expected names the populations where today holds a row the kernel does not build, and over the base there is none. A new difference fails it. It failed first with an empty chunk read as a row: 281 of the 338 fact types then differed, many holding a row today did not. ka:law reads the agreement once, ka:dir, for both its parts. MEASURED over the base: ka:dir in 208 s, each population read over the D V checks.",
DEF("ka:expected", K(PHI())),
"THE ROWS THE KERNEL HOLDS BEYOND TODAY`S. The kernel mints an involvement link for each fact type whose facts are instances, its reading with the Text and the Predicate the metamodel makes mandatory, which today`s 181 such readings lack. Each such fact type plays a role in its link, so it is an Object Type, and core.md gives each Object Type a World Assumption: 81 more than today`s, API, which objectifies Fact Type is activated by Predicate, among them. And the kernel files an Object Type Instance under each Object Type whose role it fills and under every supertype, as instances.md holds membership transitive, over every population P holds: the schema reflected as the metamodel`s facts, its constraints, spans, readings and roles; each fact of a fact type with a link under that fact type; and each entity`s id under its popular reference mode`s value type. Today`s reflection files the extents of Fact Type, Role, Entity Type and Value Type and the instances asserted, closed over subtyping. MEASURED over the base: 21,514 instance-of rows more than today`s, Function_id 7,243, Function 5,236, Constraint Span 2,041, Constraint 1,336, Role has Position in Reading 1,179 and Reading 598 the most, and so 6,181 properly-of and 15,333 most-specifically-of rows more. Whether a value or a fact is an Object Type Instance at all is not settled here: the kernel reads instances.md as it is written.",
DEF("ka:allowed_extra", K(S6(S2(A("ReadingHasText"), N(181)), S2(A("ReadingIsUsedByPredicate"), N(181)), S2(A("ObjectTypeHasWorldAssumption"), N(81)), S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), N(21514)), S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsProperlyOfObjectType"), N(6181)), S2(A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsMostSpecificallyOfObjectType"), N(15333))))),
