"THE CONSTRAINT AGREEMENT LAW. Today`s base is alethically clean, so every violation the kernel answers over it must be accounted for: it is of a constraint whose span reaches a fact type in ka:expected, a population where today holds a row the kernel does not build, or of a constraint ka:findings names. MEASURED: V answers 36 violations over the base, all of the constraints ka:findings names for the values today`s reader files in text. It failed first with a uniqueness that took every row for a duplicate.",
DEF("ka:v_of", S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"), S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), S3(A("COMP"), A("k:V"), A("k:boot"))))),
